    text: 'I didn’t want a voice coach that talks over your set. So the coach in Workout Director runs on a realtime model, but the phone decides when it gets to speak.\n\nThe predictable stuff, rep counts and rest countdowns, is just recorded clips. The model only hears about the moments that need a voice, such as the start, a new exercise or the end of a set.\n\nDuring a set it gets one interruption by default, for form, a stall or stepping out of frame. It stays quiet for your last three reps unless it’s about form or pain. Lines it starts on its own are spaced out too, from at least 20 seconds apart on the Hype coach style to 45 on Minimal, and the talk setting stretches or shrinks that.\n\nRest tips are never queued, so it can’t read out a rest time that has gone stale. Pain, a form break and the workout wrap-up skip the gap between lines, and pain also gets through on every coach style, past the per-set limit and past the cap on coach turns.',
