    text: 'The trainer chat in my app looks simple: you type, it answers. Most of the work is in what goes into each request and what’s allowed to come back.\n\nEvery request is built in the same order. What rarely changes goes first: the instructions, your profile, the facts the trainer has been told to remember and a summary of older chat. Then the last 24 messages, and only then what changes every turn, like today’s plan and your recent training. Keeping the stable parts up front lets the prompt cache reuse them from one message to the next.\n\nLong chats get folded down. Once there are 36 messages since the last summary, everything but the newest 24 goes into a running summary that the model is asked to keep to eight short lines.\n\nThe reply has a fixed shape too: a few replies, any memory changes, any food or training you mentioned, and, when you’ve just told it something about yourself, any change to your training profile. The prompt tells it to remember only lasting facts you actually stated, not moods or guesses.\n\nAnd if a flaky connection makes the phone send the same message twice, the backend spots the repeated id and returns the stored reply instead of asking the model again.',
